# Test: a peer block naming a four-octet AS opens with AS_TRANS in the My
# Autonomous System field and the real AS in the capability, and the session
# establishes.
#
# VALIDATES: RFC 6793 Section 3, which places AS_TRANS (23456) in the two-octet
#            field "if and only if the speaker does not have a (globally unique)
#            two-octet AS number", and RFC 6793 Section 4.1, which makes the
#            Capability Value of capability 65 the AS a receiver reads
#            (buildOpen, internal/test/peer/open.go).
# PREVENTS:  a four-octet option=asn being dropped in silence. The old builder
#            guarded both writes with `ASN > 0 && ASN <= 65535`, so a .ci asking
#            for AS 4200000000 patched NEITHER carrier and the peer opened with
#            ze's own AS.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: 4200000000 does not fit two octets, so it can reach ze through
# the capability alone. With the capability left at ze's AS, or with the request
# dropped, ze reads an AS this peer is not configured for and answers OPEN
# Message Error / Bad Peer AS: no UPDATE and no End-of-RIB arrive.
#
# R-7 in the spec: this is the only .ci in the tree that names an AS above 65535,
# so it is the only exerciser the four-octet path has.

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=asn:value=4200000000
cmd=api:conn=1:seq=1:text=send bgp * update text origin igp as-path [65533] nhop 10.0.1.254 nlri ipv4/unicast add 10.0.0.0/24
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF002F02000000144001010040020602010000FFFD4003040A0001FE180A0000
expect=json:conn=1:seq=1:json={"meta":{"version":"1.0.0","format":"ze-bgp"},"message":{"type":"update"},"peer":{"address":"127.0.0.1","remote":{"as":4200000000}},"direction":"in","as-path":[65533],"origin":"igp","ipv4/unicast":[{"action":"add","nlri":["10.0.0.0/24"],"next-hop":"10.0.1.254"}]}
cmd=api:conn=1:seq=1:text=send bgp * update text nlri ipv4/unicast eor
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER

# ze bgp configuration
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65533
				remote 4200000000
			}
			router-id 10.0.0.2
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
		timer {
			receive-hold-time 180
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				next-hop 10.0.1.254
				local-preference 200
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 10.0.0.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=10s
